---
// The 404 page CloudFront serves for any path that does not resolve.
//
// It exists because CloudFront requires ResponsePagePath and ResponseCode TOGETHER on a
// custom error response - specifying a status without a page is rejected outright at
// distribution creation ("Both or neither of ResponseCode and ResponsePagePath must be
// specified"). So an honest 404 needs a real page to point at, not just a status.
//
// This is the alternative to the blanket SPA fallback: a missing page renders THIS with a
// 404 status, rather than rendering the app shell with a 200 and looking like a page that
// failed to load.
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>Page not found | SJSU Student Success Navigator</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main>
			<h1>Page not found</h1>
			<p>That page does not exist. <a href="/">Go to the Student Success Navigator</a>.</p>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
